IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-dates`

-- Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) -- the rules a person bringing a claim for death or personal injury meets: Part 5
-- (death claims, solatium, the three-year limit), Part 6 Divisions 3 and 6 (obvious and inherent risks, criminal
-- conduct), Part 7 (contributory negligence and its fixed statutory reductions), Part 8 (damages for personal injury,
-- with the Civil Liability Regulations 2013 regs 7 and 19) and Part 9 Divisions 5, 6, 8, 11 and 12 (consortium, the
-- costs of raising a child, damages for delay, good samaritans, apologies). Seat-neutral: every rule is here, and the
-- claimant's seat (cla-seat.l4) asks the questions. Two regulative rules (s 25 and s 70(4)) are run by EVALTRACE.
--
-- Answers are named outcomes. Where the text says no in its own words the outcome is a "no: ..." naming the provision;
-- where the text leaves the matter to the general law the outcome says that the section "does not ..." (the 2026-11-04
-- and 2026-11-05 rulings in substance). A court's judgment ("satisfied", "exceptional", "harsh and unjust",
-- "reasonable") is an input, never decided here.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025 (the Act as at 22 June 2023, the Regulations as at 2 October 2015; unofficial, possibly out of date).
-- CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Liability Act 1936 -- the claimant's rules`

§§ `Dates the Act and its amending Acts fix`

-- Wrongs Act Amendment Act 1974, commenced 28 November 1974 (legislative history): ss 28(1), 29(1).
`the day the 1974 amendments commenced` MEANS `the date` 28 11 1974
-- Law Reform (Ipp Recommendations) Act 2004 Pt 2, commenced 1 May 2004; Sch 1 cl 1: prospective only. This encoding
-- covers accidents on or after that day for Parts 6, 7 and 8 (NOTES.md, scope).
`the day the Ipp amendments commenced` MEANS `the date` 1 5 2004
-- Law Reform (Delay in Resolution of Personal Injury Claims) Act 2002, s 4, commenced 10 March 2003: s 70(9).
`the day section 70 commenced` MEANS `the date` 10 3 2003
-- Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013, Sch 2, commenced 1 July 2013: ss 52(3)-(8), 56A, 58(4)-(6),
-- 58A, 58B, 65(2), and the definition of MVA motor accident; Sch 2 cl 21(2): earlier causes of action are not affected.
`the day the MVA rules commenced` MEANS `the date` 1 7 2013

§§ `Part 5 -- Wrongful acts or neglect causing death`

-- s 3(1): spouse (legally married on the day the cause of action arose); domestic partner (declared under the Family
-- Relationships Act 1975, or in a registered relationship, on that day); parent includes grandparents and step-parents;
-- brother and sister include half- and step-; child includes grandchildren and step-children.
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `the spouse`
    `the domestic partner`
    `the father or mother`
    `a grandparent or step-parent`
    `a brother or sister, including a half- or step-brother or sister`
    `a child, grandchild or step-child`
    `none of these`

GIVEN r IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE r `is a person section 24(1) names` IF
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Death action benefit answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the action for the death is brought for your benefit (s 24(1))`
    `the action need not be brought for your benefit: you renounced it by written notice served on the executor or administrator (s 24(5))`
    `no: the action is for the spouse, domestic partner, parent, brother, sister and child of the deceased only (s 24(1))`

-- s 24(1), (5).
GIVEN r IS A `Relationship to the deceased`, `renounced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Death action benefit answer`
`is the death action for my benefit (s 24(1), (5))` r `renounced` MEANS
    IF NOT (r `is a person section 24(1) names`)
    THEN `no: the action is for the spouse, domestic partner, parent, brother, sister and child of the deceased only (s 24(1))`
    ELSE IF `renounced`
         THEN `the action need not be brought for your benefit: you renounced it by written notice served on the executor or administrator (s 24(5))`
         ELSE `yes: the action for the death is brought for your benefit (s 24(1))`

-- s 25 ("within three years after the death") and s 27(1) ("within six months after the death"), fork F1.
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence the Part 5 action (s 25)` `the day of death` MEANS `the day of death` `plus months` 36

-- s 70(4): "within 3 years after the deceased person's death" (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to bring the section 70 claim (s 70(4))` `the day of death` MEANS `the day of death` `plus months` 36

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the six months after the death (s 27(1))` `the day of death` MEANS `the day of death` `plus months` 6

DECLARE `Who may bring the death action answer` IS ONE OF
    `you may bring it yourself: there is no executor or administrator (s 27(1))`
    `you may bring it yourself: no action under Part 5 was commenced within six months after the death (s 27(1))`
    `not yet: the executor or administrator brings it (s 24(1)); you may bring it yourself only if none is commenced within six months after the death (s 27(1))`
    `no: not more than one action lies under Part 5 for the same subject matter, and one has been commenced (s 25)`
    `no: you are not a person for whose benefit the action could be brought (ss 24(1), 27(1))`

-- s 24(1), s 25 (one action), s 27(1). "the day you would commence" is the day the person would file.
GIVEN r IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
      `there is an executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an action has been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the day you would commence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Who may bring the death action answer`
`who may bring the Part 5 action (ss 24, 25, 27)` r `there is an executor or administrator` `an action has been commenced` `the day of death` `the day you would commence` MEANS
    IF NOT (r `is a person section 24(1) names`)
    THEN `no: you are not a person for whose benefit the action could be brought (ss 24(1), 27(1))`
    ELSE IF `an action has been commenced`
         THEN `no: not more than one action lies under Part 5 for the same subject matter, and one has been commenced (s 25)`
         ELSE IF NOT `there is an executor or administrator`
              THEN `you may bring it yourself: there is no executor or administrator (s 27(1))`
              ELSE IF (`the last day of the six months after the death (s 27(1))` `the day of death`) `is before` `the day you would commence`
                   THEN `you may bring it yourself: no action under Part 5 was commenced within six months after the death (s 27(1))`
                   ELSE `not yet: the executor or administrator brings it (s 24(1)); you may bring it yourself only if none is commenced within six months after the death (s 27(1))`

§§§ `The two time limits as regulative rules`

DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF `the claimant`

DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF
    `commence the action under Part 5`
    `bring the claim under section 70 before the court or tribunal`

-- s 25: "every such action shall be commenced within three years after the death". Clock: day 0 is the day of death.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 25 -- the action for a death must be commenced within three years after the death` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the claimant`
    MUST   `commence the action under Part 5`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 25: the action was not commenced within three years after the death"

-- s 70(4): "such a claim must be brought before the court or tribunal within 3 years after the deceased person's death".
-- Clock: day 0 is the day of death.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 70(4) -- a claim for damages for unreasonable delay must be brought within 3 years after the death` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the claimant`
    MUST   `bring the claim under section 70 before the court or tribunal`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 70(4): the claim was not brought within 3 years after the death"

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED
-- means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it today would still be in
-- time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Time limit answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: it was commenced within three years after the death`
    `out of time: it was not commenced within three years after the death`
    `still in time: the three years after the death have not yet run out`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
      `the act` IS A `Claim act`
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `it has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the three-year limit` `the rule` `for` `the act` `from` `the day of death` `done` `it has been done` `on` `the day it was done` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `the act` (`the days from` `the day of death` `to` `the day it was done`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time: it was commenced within three years after the death`
         OTHERWISE `out of time: it was not commenced within three years after the death`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `the act` (`the days from` `the day of death` `to` `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still in time: the three years after the death have not yet run out`
         OTHERWISE `out of time: it was not commenced within three years after the death`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the three years after the death` `the day of death` MEANS
    `the days from` `the day of death` `to` (`the last day to commence the Part 5 action (s 25)` `the day of death`)

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE, `commenced` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day commenced` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`was the Part 5 action commenced in time (s 25)` `the day of death` `commenced` `the day commenced` `today` MEANS
    `the three-year limit` (`s 25 -- the action for a death must be commenced within three years after the death` (`the days in the three years after the death` `the day of death`)) `for` `commence the action under Part 5` `from` `the day of death` `done` `commenced` `on` `the day commenced` `as of` `today`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE, `brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day brought` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`was the section 70 claim brought in time (s 70(4))` `the day of death` `brought` `the day brought` `today` MEANS
    `the three-year limit` (`s 70(4) -- a claim for damages for unreasonable delay must be brought within 3 years after the death` (`the days in the three years after the death` `the day of death`)) `for` `bring the claim under section 70 before the court or tribunal` `from` `the day of death` `done` `brought` `on` `the day brought` `as of` `today`

§§§ `Damages for the death: what is not taken into account (s 24(2a), (2aa))`

DECLARE `Payment on the death` IS ONE OF
    `a sum under a contract of life assurance or insurance`
    `a gratuity paid because of the death`
    `superannuation payments or benefits because of the death`
    `a sum under a contributory medical, hospital, death or funeral benefit scheme`
    `a social service benefit or pension from the Commonwealth, the United Kingdom or South Australia`
    `damages recovered for the estate under s 3(2) of the Survival of Causes of Action Act 1940 (dust disease)`
    `another payment`

DECLARE `Deduction answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: it is not taken into account in assessing the damages for the death (s 24(2aa))`
    `s 24(2aa) does not exclude it: whether it is taken into account is left to the general law`

GIVEN p IS A `Payment on the death`
GIVETH A `Deduction answer`
`is this payment taken into account (s 24(2aa))` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `another payment` THEN `s 24(2aa) does not exclude it: whether it is taken into account is left to the general law`
    OTHERWISE `no: it is not taken into account in assessing the damages for the death (s 24(2aa))`

DECLARE `Expenses answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: damages may be awarded for the medical expenses of the injury that caused the death and the funeral expenses (s 24(2a))`
    `no: s 24(2a) covers only medical and funeral expenses incurred by the persons for whose benefit the action is brought`

GIVEN `incurred by a person for whose benefit the action is brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Expenses answer`
`can the damages include medical and funeral expenses (s 24(2a))` `incurred by a person for whose benefit the action is brought` MEANS
    IF `incurred by a person for whose benefit the action is brought`
    THEN `yes: damages may be awarded for the medical expenses of the injury that caused the death and the funeral expenses (s 24(2a))`
    ELSE `no: s 24(2a) covers only medical and funeral expenses incurred by the persons for whose benefit the action is brought`

§§§ `Solatium (ss 28-30)`

DECLARE `Solatium answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` HAS `the most` IS A NUMBER
    `no: solatium under s 28 is for the father or mother of a child who was an infant (s 28(1), (4))`
    `no: solatium under s 29 is for the surviving spouse or domestic partner (s 29(1))`
    `no: the death was not caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default that would have entitled the deceased to sue (ss 28(1), 29(1))`
    `no: the court has refused it, having regard to your conduct or relations with the deceased or another sufficient reason (s 30(2))`
    `the Act sets no maximum for a death on 28 November 1974, the day the 1974 amendments commenced (ss 28(1), 29(1))`

-- ss 28(1), 29(1): the maximum by the day of death. "before" and "after" the commencement leave the day itself.
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE, `the earlier maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the solatium maximum for` `the day of death` `with earlier maximum` `the earlier maximum` MEANS
    IF `the day of death` `is before` `the day the 1974 amendments commenced`
    THEN JUST `the earlier maximum`
    ELSE IF `the day the 1974 amendments commenced` `is before` `the day of death`
         THEN JUST 10000
         ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the maximum` IS A MAYBE NUMBER, `wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court refuses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Solatium answer`
`the solatium answer for` `the maximum` `wrongful` `the court refuses` MEANS
    IF NOT `wrongful`
    THEN `no: the death was not caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default that would have entitled the deceased to sue (ss 28(1), 29(1))`
    ELSE IF `the court refuses`
         THEN `no: the court has refused it, having regard to your conduct or relations with the deceased or another sufficient reason (s 30(2))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the maximum`
              WHEN JUST m THEN `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` m
              WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Act sets no maximum for a death on 28 November 1974, the day the 1974 amendments commenced (ss 28(1), 29(1))`

-- s 28: the father or mother (s 28(4)) of an infant (a borrowed term, asked). The maximum is for the parents together
-- (s 28(2) divides what is recovered between them).
GIVEN `I am the father or mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child was an infant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the court refuses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Solatium answer`
`solatium for the death of a child (s 28)` `I am the father or mother` `the child was an infant` `wrongful` `the day of death` `the court refuses` MEANS
    IF NOT (`I am the father or mother` AND `the child was an infant`)
    THEN `no: solatium under s 28 is for the father or mother of a child who was an infant (s 28(1), (4))`
    ELSE `the solatium answer for` (`the solatium maximum for` `the day of death` `with earlier maximum` 1000) `wrongful` `the court refuses`

-- s 29: the surviving spouse or domestic partner. Where both claim, the total stays at the single maximum (s 29(2)).
GIVEN r IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
      `wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the court refuses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Solatium answer`
`solatium for the death of a spouse or domestic partner (s 29)` r `wrongful` `the day of death` `the court refuses` MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the spouse` THEN `the solatium answer for` (`the solatium maximum for` `the day of death` `with earlier maximum` 1400) `wrongful` `the court refuses`
    WHEN `the domestic partner` THEN `the solatium answer for` (`the solatium maximum for` `the day of death` `with earlier maximum` 1400) `wrongful` `the court refuses`
    OTHERWISE `no: solatium under s 29 is for the surviving spouse or domestic partner (s 29(1))`

§§ `Part 6 -- Negligence: obvious and inherent risks, criminal conduct`

DECLARE `Awareness answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the defence fails, because a reasonable person in your position would not have taken steps to avoid the risk (s 37(3))`
    `you are taken to have been aware of the risk (s 37(1)); the defence may then succeed`
    `you are not taken to have been aware of it: you proved you were not actually aware of the risk (s 37(1))`
    `s 37(1) does not apply: the risk was not an obvious risk, so your awareness is left to the general law`
    `s 37 does not apply: the defendant has not raised voluntary assumption of risk`

-- s 37. "obvious risk" (s 36) and "a reasonable person ... would have taken steps" (s 37(3)) are the court's: inputs.
GIVEN `raised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk was obvious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable person would have taken steps you did not take` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you prove you were not actually aware` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Awareness answer`
`voluntary assumption of an obvious risk (s 37)` `raised` `the risk was obvious` `a reasonable person would have taken steps you did not take` `you prove you were not actually aware` MEANS
    IF NOT `raised`
    THEN `s 37 does not apply: the defendant has not raised voluntary assumption of risk`
    ELSE IF NOT `a reasonable person would have taken steps you did not take`
         THEN `no: the defence fails, because a reasonable person in your position would not have taken steps to avoid the risk (s 37(3))`
         ELSE IF NOT `the risk was obvious`
              THEN `s 37(1) does not apply: the risk was not an obvious risk, so your awareness is left to the general law`
              ELSE IF `you prove you were not actually aware`
                   THEN `you are not taken to have been aware of it: you proved you were not actually aware of the risk (s 37(1))`
                   ELSE `you are taken to have been aware of the risk (s 37(1)); the defence may then succeed`

DECLARE `Duty to warn answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: there is no duty to warn you of an obvious risk (s 38(1))`
    `s 38(1) does not apply, but that raises no presumption of a duty to warn; the general law decides (s 38(2), (3))`
    `s 38 does not deal with a risk that was not obvious`

-- s 38.
GIVEN `the risk was obvious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you asked for advice or information about the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law required the warning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a risk of death or injury from a health care service the defendant provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty to warn answer`
`duty to warn of an obvious risk (s 38)` `the risk was obvious` `you asked for advice or information about the risk` `a written law required the warning` `a risk of death or injury from a health care service the defendant provided` MEANS
    IF NOT `the risk was obvious`
    THEN `s 38 does not deal with a risk that was not obvious`
    ELSE IF `you asked for advice or information about the risk` OR `a written law required the warning` OR `a risk of death or injury from a health care service the defendant provided`
         THEN `s 38(1) does not apply, but that raises no presumption of a duty to warn; the general law decides (s 38(2), (3))`
         ELSE `no: there is no duty to warn you of an obvious risk (s 38(1))`

DECLARE `Inherent risk answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: there is no liability in negligence for harm from the materialisation of an inherent risk (s 39(1))`
    `s 39 does not exclude liability for failing to warn of the risk (s 39(3))`
    `s 39 does not apply: the risk could have been avoided by reasonable care and skill`

-- s 39. Whether the risk "cannot be avoided by the exercise of reasonable care and skill" is the court's: an input.
GIVEN `the risk could not be avoided by reasonable care and skill` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claim is for failing to warn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Inherent risk answer`
`inherent risk (s 39)` `the risk could not be avoided by reasonable care and skill` `the claim is for failing to warn` MEANS
    IF NOT `the risk could not be avoided by reasonable care and skill`
    THEN `s 39 does not apply: the risk could have been avoided by reasonable care and skill`
    ELSE IF `the claim is for failing to warn`
         THEN `s 39 does not exclude liability for failing to warn of the risk (s 39(3))`
         ELSE `no: there is no liability in negligence for harm from the materialisation of an inherent risk (s 39(1))`

§§§ `Where Part 8 and s 43 apply (ss 43(4), 51)`

DECLARE `How the injury arose` IS ONE OF
    `in an MVA motor accident`
    `in another motor accident`
    `in an accident caused wholly or partly by negligence, another person's unintentional tort, or a breach of a contractual duty of care`
    `in some other way`

GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 8 applies to an injury arising` how IF
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `in some other way` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`, `the accident day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the MVA rules apply to an injury arising` how `on` `the accident day` IF
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `in an MVA motor accident` THEN `the day the MVA rules commenced` `is on or before` `the accident day`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accident is within this encoding` `the accident day` IF `the day the Ipp amendments commenced` `is on or before` `the accident day`

DECLARE `Offence finding` IS ONE OF
    `you were convicted of the offence`
    `you were acquitted of the offence`
    `no conviction or acquittal, and the court is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that you were committing it`
    `no conviction or acquittal, and the court is not so satisfied`

DECLARE `Criminal conduct answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: your claim for damages is excluded, because the accident happened while you were committing an indictable offence that contributed materially to the risk of injury (s 43(1))`
    `the exclusion applies, but the court may still award damages because the case is exceptional and the exclusion would operate harshly and unjustly (s 43(2))`
    `s 43 does not exclude your claim`
    `s 43 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 43(4))`

-- s 43. A conviction or acquittal is conclusive (s 43(3)).
GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`
      `the finding` IS A `Offence finding`
      `your conduct contributed materially to the risk of injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exceptional and harsh and unjust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Criminal conduct answer`
`exclusion for criminal conduct (s 43)` how `the finding` `your conduct contributed materially to the risk of injury` `exceptional and harsh and unjust` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part 8 applies to an injury arising` how)
    THEN `s 43 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 43(4))`
    ELSE IF `committing an indictable offence` AND `your conduct contributed materially to the risk of injury`
         THEN IF `exceptional and harsh and unjust`
              THEN `the exclusion applies, but the court may still award damages because the case is exceptional and the exclusion would operate harshly and unjustly (s 43(2))`
              ELSE `no: your claim for damages is excluded, because the accident happened while you were committing an indictable offence that contributed materially to the risk of injury (s 43(1))`
         ELSE `s 43 does not exclude your claim`
    WHERE
        `committing an indictable offence` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the finding`
            WHEN `you were convicted of the offence` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `no conviction or acquittal, and the court is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that you were committing it` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Part 7 -- Contributory negligence`

-- s 48(1): a blood alcohol concentration of .08 grams or more in 100 millilitres found by a court is conclusive of
-- intoxication. s 46(4), 47(5): .15 grams or more raises the reduction to 50 per cent.
GIVEN `the concentration found` IS A NUMBER, `intoxicated otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `intoxicated (ss 3, 48(1))` `the concentration found` `intoxicated otherwise` IF
    `the concentration found` AT LEAST 0.08 OR `intoxicated otherwise`

GIVEN `the concentration found` IS A NUMBER, `incapable of effective control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the higher level (ss 46(4), 47(5))` `the concentration found` `incapable of effective control` IF
    `the concentration found` AT LEAST 0.15 OR `incapable of effective control`

DECLARE `Intoxication answer` IS ONE OF
    `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` HAS `the per cent` IS A NUMBER
    `the presumption is rebutted (s 46(2)); an ordinary finding of contributory negligence is still possible`
    `s 46 raises no presumption: you were not intoxicated, or the defendant does not allege contributory negligence`

-- s 46. The minimum reduction is 25 per cent, or 50 per cent for a driver at the higher level in a motor accident.
GIVEN `the concentration found` IS A NUMBER
      `intoxicated otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contributory negligence is alleged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intoxication did not contribute to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intoxication was not self-induced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `wholly prescribed drugs taken as instructed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you were the driver in a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `incapable of effective control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Intoxication answer`
`your own intoxication (s 46)` `the concentration found` `intoxicated otherwise` `contributory negligence is alleged` `the intoxication did not contribute to the accident` `the intoxication was not self-induced` `wholly prescribed drugs taken as instructed` `you were the driver in a motor accident` `incapable of effective control` MEANS
    IF NOT (`intoxicated (ss 3, 48(1))` `the concentration found` `intoxicated otherwise` AND `contributory negligence is alleged`)
    THEN `s 46 raises no presumption: you were not intoxicated, or the defendant does not allege contributory negligence`
    ELSE IF `the intoxication did not contribute to the accident` OR `the intoxication was not self-induced` OR `wholly prescribed drugs taken as instructed`
         THEN `the presumption is rebutted (s 46(2)); an ordinary finding of contributory negligence is still possible`
         ELSE IF `you were the driver in a motor accident` AND `the higher level (ss 46(4), 47(5))` `the concentration found` `incapable of effective control`
              THEN `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` 50
              ELSE `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` 25

DECLARE `Fixed reduction answer` IS ONE OF
    `a fixed statutory reduction of` HAS `the per cent` IS A NUMBER
    `the presumption is rebutted: no fixed reduction`
    `no presumption under this section`

-- s 47. A passenger in a motor vehicle is taken to rely on the driver (s 47(4)).
GIVEN `your age at the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `you relied on the person's care and skill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you were a passenger in the motor vehicle the person drove` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's concentration found` IS A NUMBER
      `the person was otherwise intoxicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you were aware or ought to have been aware` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's negligence caused the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contributory negligence is alleged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intoxication did not contribute to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you could not reasonably be expected to have avoided the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the driver was incapable of effective control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Fixed reduction answer`
`relying on an intoxicated person (s 47)` `your age at the accident` `you relied on the person's care and skill` `you were a passenger in the motor vehicle the person drove` `the person's concentration found` `the person was otherwise intoxicated` `you were aware or ought to have been aware` `the person's negligence caused the accident` `contributory negligence is alleged` `the intoxication did not contribute to the accident` `you could not reasonably be expected to have avoided the risk` `a motor accident` `the driver was incapable of effective control` MEANS
    IF NOT (`presumed`)
    THEN `no presumption under this section`
    ELSE IF `the intoxication did not contribute to the accident` OR `you could not reasonably be expected to have avoided the risk`
         THEN `the presumption is rebutted: no fixed reduction`
         ELSE IF `a motor accident` AND `the higher level (ss 46(4), 47(5))` `the person's concentration found` `the driver was incapable of effective control`
              THEN `a fixed statutory reduction of` 50
              ELSE `a fixed statutory reduction of` 25
    WHERE
        `presumed` MEANS
                `your age at the accident` AT LEAST 16
            AND (`you relied on the person's care and skill` OR `you were a passenger in the motor vehicle the person drove`)
            AND `intoxicated (ss 3, 48(1))` `the person's concentration found` `the person was otherwise intoxicated`
            AND `you were aware or ought to have been aware`
            AND `the person's negligence caused the accident`
            AND `contributory negligence is alleged`

-- s 49. Only the passenger-compartment case can be rebutted (s 49(2)).
GIVEN `injured in a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `your age at the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `not wearing a seatbelt as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not wearing a safety helmet as required, and that contributed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a passenger outside the passenger compartment, and that contributed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you could not reasonably be expected to have avoided the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Fixed reduction answer`
`seatbelt, helmet or passenger compartment (s 49)` `injured in a motor accident` `your age at the accident` `not wearing a seatbelt as required` `not wearing a safety helmet as required, and that contributed` `a passenger outside the passenger compartment, and that contributed` `you could not reasonably be expected to have avoided the risk` MEANS
    IF NOT (`injured in a motor accident` AND `your age at the accident` AT LEAST 16)
    THEN `no presumption under this section`
    ELSE IF `not wearing a seatbelt as required` OR `not wearing a safety helmet as required, and that contributed`
         THEN `a fixed statutory reduction of` 25
         ELSE IF `a passenger outside the passenger compartment, and that contributed`
              THEN IF `you could not reasonably be expected to have avoided the risk`
                   THEN `the presumption is rebutted: no fixed reduction`
                   ELSE `a fixed statutory reduction of` 25
              ELSE `no presumption under this section`

GIVEN a IS A `Fixed reduction answer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the per cent of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `a fixed statutory reduction of` p THEN p
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN a IS A `Intoxication answer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum per cent of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` p THEN p
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 50(2)-(4): first the full damages; second the court's percentage for actual contributory negligence (including
-- intoxication), never below the intoxication minimum; third the fixed statutory reductions, in series.
GIVEN `the full damages` IS A NUMBER
      `the court's percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the intoxication minimum` IS A NUMBER
      `the first fixed reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the second fixed reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the damages after contributory negligence (s 50)` `the full damages` `the court's percentage` `the intoxication minimum` `the first fixed reduction` `the second fixed reduction` MEANS
    ((`the full damages` `reduced by per cent` (`the larger of` `the court's percentage` `and` `the intoxication minimum`)) `reduced by per cent` `the first fixed reduction`) `reduced by per cent` `the second fixed reduction`

§§ `Part 8 -- Damages for personal injury`

§§§ `Prescribed minimum and maximum (s 3(1)), indexed amounts (s 52(2)(d), (7)), reg 7`

-- s 3(1) prescribed minimum and maximum: for 2002 the stated sum; later, the sum times CPI (September quarter of the
-- preceding year) over CPI (September quarter 2001), to the nearest $10.
GIVEN `the sum for 2002` IS A NUMBER
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed sum` `the sum for 2002` `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2001` MEANS
    IF DATE_YEAR `the accident day` AT MOST 2002
    THEN `the sum for 2002`
    ELSE `to the nearest multiple of $10` (`the sum for 2002` TIMES (`CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` DIVIDED BY `CPI September quarter 2001`))

-- s 52(7), (8): "(indexed)" amounts adjusted each 1 July from 1 July 2014 by CPI (March quarter of that year) over CPI
-- (March quarter 2013), to the nearest $10; the amount applying at the time of the injury. Before 1 July 2014, unadjusted.
GIVEN `the stated amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indexed (s 52(7))` `the stated amount` `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` `and` `CPI March quarter 2013` MEANS
    IF `the accident day` `is before` (`the date` 1 7 2014)
    THEN `the stated amount`
    ELSE `to the nearest multiple of $10` (`the stated amount` TIMES (`CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` DIVIDED BY `CPI March quarter 2013`))

-- Civil Liability Regulations 2013 reg 7: an ISV is a whole number, a fraction of half or more rounded up.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`as a whole number (reg 7)` x MEANS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

§§§ `Non-economic loss (s 52)`

-- s 52(2)(c): the 2003 amounts, scale 0 to 60.
GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2003 amount for scale value` s MEANS
    BRANCH IF s AT MOST 10 THEN s TIMES 1150
           IF s AT MOST 20 THEN 11500 PLUS ((s MINUS 10) TIMES 2300)
           IF s AT MOST 30 THEN 34500 PLUS ((s MINUS 20) TIMES 3450)
           IF s AT MOST 40 THEN 69000 PLUS ((s MINUS 30) TIMES 4600)
           IF s AT MOST 50 THEN 115000 PLUS ((s MINUS 40) TIMES 5750)
           OTHERWISE 172500 PLUS ((s MINUS 50) TIMES 6900)

-- s 52(2)(b)-(d): by the year of the accident.
GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter 2002` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 52(2) amount for scale value` s `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2002` MEANS
    IF DATE_YEAR `the accident day` AT MOST 2002
    THEN s TIMES 1710
    ELSE IF DATE_YEAR `the accident day` EQUALS 2003
         THEN `the 2003 amount for scale value` s
         ELSE `to the nearest multiple of $10` (`the 2003 amount for scale value` s TIMES (`CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` DIVIDED BY `CPI September quarter 2002`))

-- s 52(3)(c): the MVA amounts, injury scale value 11 to 100, each "(indexed)" amount indexed by itself.
GIVEN v IS A NUMBER
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 52(3) amount for injury scale value` v `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` `and` `CPI March quarter 2013` MEANS
    BRANCH IF v AT MOST 31 THEN (ix 2000) PLUS ((v MINUS 10) TIMES (ix 1000))
           IF v AT MOST 45 THEN (ix 23000) PLUS ((v MINUS 31) TIMES (ix 3000))
           IF v AT MOST 66 THEN (ix 65000) PLUS ((v MINUS 45) TIMES (ix 5000))
           IF v AT MOST 78 THEN (ix 170000) PLUS ((v MINUS 66) TIMES (ix 10000))
           OTHERWISE ix 300000
    WHERE
        ix a MEANS `indexed (s 52(7))` a `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` `and` `CPI March quarter 2013`

DECLARE `Non-economic loss answer` IS ONE OF
    `damages for non-economic loss of` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `no: your ability to lead a normal life was not significantly impaired for at least 7 days, and your medical expenses were less than the prescribed minimum (s 52(1))`
    `no: your injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(4))`
    `the court may award damages although your injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(5)), but s 52(3)(c) states no amount for a value of 10 or less`
    `not a scale value: the scale runs from 0 to 60 (s 52(2)(a))`
    `not an injury scale value: the scale runs from 0 to 100 (s 52(3)(a))`
    `not covered: Part 8 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 51)`
    `not covered: an accident before 1 May 2004`

-- s 52. "significantly impaired ... for a period of at least 7 days" and "reasonably incurred" are inputs.
GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `significantly impaired for at least 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `medical expenses reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER
      `the scale value` IS A NUMBER
      `exceptional and harsh and unjust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter 2002` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Non-economic loss answer`
`damages for non-economic loss (s 52)` how `the accident day` `significantly impaired for at least 7 days` `medical expenses reasonably incurred` `the scale value` `exceptional and harsh and unjust` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI September quarter 2001` `CPI September quarter 2002` `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` `CPI March quarter 2013` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part 8 applies to an injury arising` how)
    THEN `not covered: Part 8 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 51)`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the accident is within this encoding` `the accident day`)
         THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 May 2004`
         ELSE IF NOT (`significantly impaired for at least 7 days` OR `medical expenses reasonably incurred` AT LEAST `the prescribed minimum`)
              THEN `no: your ability to lead a normal life was not significantly impaired for at least 7 days, and your medical expenses were less than the prescribed minimum (s 52(1))`
              ELSE IF `the MVA rules apply to an injury arising` how `on` `the accident day`
                   THEN `the MVA answer`
                   ELSE `the other answer`
    WHERE
        `the prescribed minimum` MEANS `the prescribed sum` 2750 `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2001`
        `the ISV` MEANS `as a whole number (reg 7)` `the scale value`
        `the MVA answer` MEANS
            IF `the ISV` LESS THAN 0 OR `the ISV` GREATER THAN 100
            THEN `not an injury scale value: the scale runs from 0 to 100 (s 52(3)(a))`
            ELSE IF `the ISV` GREATER THAN 10
                 THEN `damages for non-economic loss of` (`the s 52(3) amount for injury scale value` `the ISV` `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` `and` `CPI March quarter 2013`)
                 ELSE IF `exceptional and harsh and unjust`
                      THEN `the court may award damages although your injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(5)), but s 52(3)(c) states no amount for a value of 10 or less`
                      ELSE `no: your injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(4))`
        `the other answer` MEANS
            IF `the scale value` LESS THAN 0 OR `the scale value` GREATER THAN 60
            THEN `not a scale value: the scale runs from 0 to 60 (s 52(2)(a))`
            ELSE `damages for non-economic loss of` (`the s 52(2) amount for scale value` `the scale value` `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2002`)

§§§ `Mental harm (s 53)`

DECLARE `Kind of mental harm` IS ONE OF
    `pure mental harm`
    `consequential mental harm`

DECLARE `Mental harm answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 53 does not bar damages for this mental harm`
    `s 53 does not bar damages for this mental harm, but none may be awarded for economic loss resulting from it, because it is not a recognised psychiatric illness (s 53(3))`
    `no: you were not physically injured in the accident or present at the scene when it happened, and are not a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in it (s 53(1))`
    `no: damages for pure mental harm need a recognised psychiatric illness (s 53(2))`
    `not covered: Part 8 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 51)`
    `not covered: an accident before 1 May 2004`

GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `physically injured in the accident or present at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of mental harm`
      `a recognised psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Mental harm answer`
`damages for mental harm (s 53)` how `the accident day` `physically injured in the accident or present at the scene` `a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in it` `the kind` `a recognised psychiatric illness` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part 8 applies to an injury arising` how)
    THEN `not covered: Part 8 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 51)`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the accident is within this encoding` `the accident day`)
         THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 May 2004`
         ELSE IF NOT (`physically injured in the accident or present at the scene` OR `a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in it`)
              THEN `no: you were not physically injured in the accident or present at the scene when it happened, and are not a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in it (s 53(1))`
              ELSE IF `a recognised psychiatric illness`
                   THEN `s 53 does not bar damages for this mental harm`
                   ELSE CONSIDER `the kind`
                        WHEN `pure mental harm` THEN `no: damages for pure mental harm need a recognised psychiatric illness (s 53(2))`
                        WHEN `consequential mental harm` THEN `s 53 does not bar damages for this mental harm, but none may be awarded for economic loss resulting from it, because it is not a recognised psychiatric illness (s 53(3))`

§§§ `Loss of earning capacity (ss 54, 55, 56A)`

-- s 54(2): total damages for loss of earning capacity cannot exceed the prescribed maximum ($2.2 million, indexed).
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed maximum for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2001` MEANS
    `the prescribed sum` 2200000 `for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2001`

-- s 3(1) prescribed discount rate: 5 per cent unless a regulation fixes another; the deposited Regulations fix none.
`the prescribed discount rate (s 3(1), s 55)` MEANS 5

DECLARE `Future earning capacity answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 56A(2) does not bar damages for loss of future earning capacity`
    `the court may award damages for loss of future earning capacity although your injury scale value is 7 or less, because the consequences are exceptional and the threshold harsh and unjust (s 56A(3))`
    `no: after an MVA motor accident, damages for loss or impairment of future earning capacity need an injury scale value over 7 (s 56A(2))`

GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `the scale value` IS A NUMBER
      `exceptional and harsh and unjust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Future earning capacity answer`
`the threshold for future earning capacity (s 56A(2), (3))` how `the accident day` `the scale value` `exceptional and harsh and unjust` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the MVA rules apply to an injury arising` how `on` `the accident day`)
    THEN `s 56A(2) does not bar damages for loss of future earning capacity`
    ELSE IF `as a whole number (reg 7)` `the scale value` GREATER THAN 7
         THEN `s 56A(2) does not bar damages for loss of future earning capacity`
         ELSE IF `exceptional and harsh and unjust`
              THEN `the court may award damages for loss of future earning capacity although your injury scale value is 7 or less, because the consequences are exceptional and the threshold harsh and unjust (s 56A(3))`
              ELSE `no: after an MVA motor accident, damages for loss or impairment of future earning capacity need an injury scale value over 7 (s 56A(2))`

-- s 54(1)-(2) and s 56A(5), fork F3: the cap is applied first, then the further 20% for an MVA motor accident.
-- `the assessed damages` leave out the first week of incapacity (s 54(1)) and interest on past loss, and are after the
-- discount rate and any reduction for contributory negligence.
GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `the assessed damages` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the damages for loss of earning capacity (ss 54(2), 56A(5))` how `the accident day` `the assessed damages` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI September quarter 2001` MEANS
    IF `the MVA rules apply to an injury arising` how `on` `the accident day`
    THEN `the capped` `reduced by per cent` 20
    ELSE `the capped`
    WHERE
        `the capped` MEANS `the smaller of` `the assessed damages` `and` (`the prescribed maximum for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2001`)

-- s 54(3): for dependants, economic loss from the death (apart from expenses actually incurred) is capped at the
-- prescribed maximum, less damages the deceased received for loss of earning capacity before death.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `damages the deceased received for loss of earning capacity` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI September quarter 2001` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most for dependants' economic loss (s 54(3))` `the accident day` `damages the deceased received for loss of earning capacity` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `CPI September quarter 2001` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 `and` ((`the prescribed maximum for` `the accident day` `with` `CPI September quarter of the year before the accident` `and` `CPI September quarter 2001`) MINUS `damages the deceased received for loss of earning capacity`)

-- s 56A(6)-(9): lost superannuation contributions after an MVA motor accident, at most the relevant percentage (the
-- minimum employer contribution rate the law requires, a borrowed figure) of the earning capacity damages.
GIVEN `the earning capacity damages` IS A NUMBER, `the relevant percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most for lost superannuation contributions (s 56A(6), (8))` `the earning capacity damages` `the relevant percentage` MEANS
    `the earning capacity damages` TIMES (`the relevant percentage` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 58B(3): loss of financial support after a death in an MVA motor accident, a further 20%.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the assessed damages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the damages for loss of financial support (s 58B(3))` `the accident day` `the assessed damages` MEANS
    IF `the MVA rules apply to an injury arising` `in an MVA motor accident` `on` `the accident day`
    THEN `the assessed damages` `reduced by per cent` 20
    ELSE `the assessed damages`

§§§ `Interest and management costs (ss 56, 57)`

DECLARE `Head of damages` IS ONE OF
    `non-economic loss`
    `future loss`
    `past economic loss`
    `the cost of investing or managing the award`

DECLARE `Interest answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: interest is not awarded on damages for non-economic or future loss (s 56)`
    `no: damages are not awarded for the cost of investing or managing the amount awarded (s 57)`
    `ss 56 and 57 do not exclude interest on damages for past economic loss`

GIVEN h IS A `Head of damages`
GIVETH A `Interest answer`
`interest on this head (ss 56, 57)` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `non-economic loss` THEN `no: interest is not awarded on damages for non-economic or future loss (s 56)`
    WHEN `future loss` THEN `no: interest is not awarded on damages for non-economic or future loss (s 56)`
    WHEN `past economic loss` THEN `ss 56 and 57 do not exclude interest on damages for past economic loss`
    WHEN `the cost of investing or managing the award` THEN `no: damages are not awarded for the cost of investing or managing the amount awarded (s 57)`

§§§ `Gratuitous services (s 58, reg 19) and the Lifetime Support Scheme (s 58A)`

DECLARE `Who gives the services` IS ONE OF
    `your parent, spouse, domestic partner or child`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Gratuitous services answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: damages for the services, up to 4 times State average weekly earnings, that is` HAS `the limit` IS A NUMBER
    `yes: damages for the services above 4 times State average weekly earnings, at a rate no higher than State average weekly earnings, that is per week at most` HAS `the weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
    `no: damages are not awarded for gratuitous services except those of a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child (s 58(1)(a))`
    `no: after an MVA motor accident, the injury scale value must exceed 10 and the services be given for at least 6 hours a week for at least 6 consecutive months (s 58(4)(a))`
    `no: as a Lifetime Support Scheme participant, not for services meeting your assessed treatment, care and support needs from the injury (s 58(5))`
    `not covered: Part 8 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 51)`
    `not covered: an accident before 1 May 2004`

-- s 58(1)-(5). State average weekly earnings (reg 18: the ABS male full-time adult ordinary time earnings for South
-- Australia) is an input. Fork F4: "4 times State average weekly earnings" read as 4 times the weekly figure.
GIVEN how IS A `How the injury arose`
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `who` IS A `Who gives the services`
      `the scale value` IS A NUMBER
      `hours a week` IS A NUMBER
      `consecutive months` IS A NUMBER
      `the services meet assessed needs as a scheme participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonably required and someone would otherwise have to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `State average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Gratuitous services answer`
`damages for gratuitous services (s 58)` how `the accident day` `who` `the scale value` `hours a week` `consecutive months` `the services meet assessed needs as a scheme participant` `reasonably required and someone would otherwise have to be paid` `State average weekly earnings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part 8 applies to an injury arising` how)
    THEN `not covered: Part 8 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 51)`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the accident is within this encoding` `the accident day`)
         THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 May 2004`
         ELSE CONSIDER `who`
              WHEN `someone else` THEN `no: damages are not awarded for gratuitous services except those of a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child (s 58(1)(a))`
              WHEN `your parent, spouse, domestic partner or child` THEN
                  IF `the MVA rules apply to an injury arising` how `on` `the accident day` AND NOT (`the MVA thresholds are met`)
                  THEN `no: after an MVA motor accident, the injury scale value must exceed 10 and the services be given for at least 6 hours a week for at least 6 consecutive months (s 58(4)(a))`
                  ELSE IF `the services meet assessed needs as a scheme participant`
                       THEN `no: as a Lifetime Support Scheme participant, not for services meeting your assessed treatment, care and support needs from the injury (s 58(5))`
                       ELSE IF `reasonably required and someone would otherwise have to be paid`
                            THEN `yes: damages for the services above 4 times State average weekly earnings, at a rate no higher than State average weekly earnings, that is per week at most` `State average weekly earnings`
                            ELSE `yes: damages for the services, up to 4 times State average weekly earnings, that is` (4 TIMES `State average weekly earnings`)
    WHERE
        `the MVA thresholds are met` MEANS
                `as a whole number (reg 7)` `the scale value` GREATER THAN 10
            AND `hours a week` AT LEAST 6
            AND `consecutive months` AT LEAST 6

-- s 58(4)(b), reg 19: $25 an hour (indexed) for an MVA motor accident. Reg 19(2) states no rounding (finding 5).
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI March quarter 2013` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the highest hourly rate for family care (s 58(4)(b), reg 19)` `the accident day` `CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` `CPI March quarter 2013` MEANS
    IF `the accident day` `is before` (`the date` 1 7 2014)
    THEN 25
    ELSE 25 TIMES (`CPI March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` DIVIDED BY `CPI March quarter 2013`)

DECLARE `Scheme answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: no damages for treatment, care and support needs from the injury that arise while you are a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme (s 58A)`
    `s 58A does not bar these damages`

GIVEN `a participant or interim participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the needs relate to the injury and arise during participation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Scheme answer`
`the Lifetime Support Scheme bar (s 58A)` `a participant or interim participant` `the needs relate to the injury and arise during participation` MEANS
    IF `a participant or interim participant` AND `the needs relate to the injury and arise during participation`
    THEN `no: no damages for treatment, care and support needs from the injury that arise while you are a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme (s 58A)`
    ELSE `s 58A does not bar these damages`

§§ `Part 9 -- Consortium, raising a child, delay, good samaritans, apologies`

DECLARE `Consortium answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the wrongdoer is liable to you for the loss or impairment of consortium (s 65(1))`
    `no: after an MVA motor accident, damages for loss of consortium need an injury scale value over 10 (s 65(2))`
    `no: s 65 is for the spouse or domestic partner of the injured person`
    `no: s 65 needs an injury caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default`

GIVEN `you are the spouse or domestic partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `How the injury arose`
      `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `the scale value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Consortium answer`
`loss of consortium (s 65)` `you are the spouse or domestic partner` `wrongful` how `the accident day` `the scale value` MEANS
    IF NOT `you are the spouse or domestic partner`
    THEN `no: s 65 is for the spouse or domestic partner of the injured person`
    ELSE IF NOT `wrongful`
         THEN `no: s 65 needs an injury caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default`
         ELSE IF `the MVA rules apply to an injury arising` how `on` `the accident day` AND `as a whole number (reg 7)` `the scale value` AT MOST 10
              THEN `no: after an MVA motor accident, damages for loss of consortium need an injury scale value over 10 (s 65(2))`
              ELSE `yes: the wrongdoer is liable to you for the loss or impairment of consortium (s 65(1))`

DECLARE `Kind of action about a child` IS ONE OF
    `negligence resulting in the unintended conception of a child`
    `negligence resulting in the failure of an attempted abortion`
    `negligence resulting in a birth from a pregnancy that would otherwise have been aborted`
    `innocent misrepresentation resulting in an unintended conception or such a birth`
    `breach of warranty of merchantable quality or fitness for purpose of a contraceptive device that failed`
    `another kind of action`

DECLARE `Raising a child answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: no damages for the ordinary costs of raising the child (s 67(1))`
    `no damages for the ordinary costs of raising the child (s 67(1)); the costs by which the child's disability reasonably increases them are not ordinary costs (s 67(2))`
    `s 67 does not apply to this kind of action (s 67(3))`

GIVEN `the action` IS A `Kind of action about a child`, `the child is mentally or physically disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Raising a child answer`
`the costs of raising a child (s 67)` `the action` `the child is mentally or physically disabled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `another kind of action` THEN `s 67 does not apply to this kind of action (s 67(3))`
    OTHERWISE IF `the child is mentally or physically disabled`
              THEN `no damages for the ordinary costs of raising the child (s 67(1)); the costs by which the child's disability reasonably increases them are not ordinary costs (s 67(2))`
              ELSE `no: no damages for the ordinary costs of raising the child (s 67(1))`

DECLARE `Delay damages answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: exemplary damages may be awarded against the person in default (s 70(1), (2)); paid to the dependants unless there are none or there is another good reason (s 70(7), (8))`
    `no: the conditions in s 70(2) are not all met`
    `no: s 70 applies only where the deceased died on or after 10 March 2003 (s 70(9))`
    `no: the claim was not brought within 3 years after the death (s 70(4))`

-- s 70(2)(a)-(f) and (4). "unreasonably delayed" (s 70(3)(a)) and the other conditions are inputs.
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the deceased had a right to compensation or damages for a personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased made a written claim giving the grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person unreasonably delayed it knowing, or when they ought to have known, of the risk of death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was the one claimed against, or controlled or had an interest in the defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `death came before non-economic loss was finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no damages are recoverable under s 3(2) of the Survival of Causes of Action Act 1940` IS A BOOLEAN
      `brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day brought` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Delay damages answer`
`damages for unreasonable delay (s 70)` `the day of death` `the deceased had a right to compensation or damages for a personal injury` `the deceased made a written claim giving the grounds` `the person unreasonably delayed it knowing, or when they ought to have known, of the risk of death` `the person was the one claimed against, or controlled or had an interest in the defence` `death came before non-economic loss was finally determined` `no damages are recoverable under s 3(2) of the Survival of Causes of Action Act 1940` `brought` `the day brought` `today` MEANS
    IF `the day of death` `is before` `the day section 70 commenced`
    THEN `no: s 70 applies only where the deceased died on or after 10 March 2003 (s 70(9))`
    ELSE IF NOT (    `the deceased had a right to compensation or damages for a personal injury`
                 AND `the deceased made a written claim giving the grounds`
                 AND `the person unreasonably delayed it knowing, or when they ought to have known, of the risk of death`
                 AND `the person was the one claimed against, or controlled or had an interest in the defence`
                 AND `death came before non-economic loss was finally determined`
                 AND `no damages are recoverable under s 3(2) of the Survival of Causes of Action Act 1940`)
         THEN `no: the conditions in s 70(2) are not all met`
         ELSE CONSIDER `was the section 70 claim brought in time (s 70(4))` `the day of death` `brought` `the day brought` `today`
              WHEN `out of time: it was not commenced within three years after the death` THEN `no: the claim was not brought within 3 years after the death (s 70(4))`
              OTHERWISE `yes: exemplary damages may be awarded against the person in default (s 70(1), (2)); paid to the dependants unless there are none or there is another good reason (s 70(7), (8))`

DECLARE `Good samaritan answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: a good samaritan incurs no personal civil liability for what was done in good faith and without recklessness (s 74(2))`
    `no: a medically qualified good samaritan incurs no personal civil liability for advice about emergency medical assistance (s 74(3))`
    `the immunity does not extend to a liability within compulsory third party motor vehicle insurance (s 74(4)(a))`
    `the immunity does not operate: their capacity was significantly impaired by alcohol or another recreational drug (s 74(4)(b))`
    `s 74 gives no immunity on these facts`

GIVEN `they expected no payment or other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you were apparently in need of emergency assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is about medical advice given by telephone or other telecommunication by a medically qualified person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in good faith and without recklessness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within compulsory third party motor vehicle insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significantly impaired by alcohol or another recreational drug` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Good samaritan answer`
`suing a good samaritan (s 74)` `they expected no payment or other consideration` `you were apparently in need of emergency assistance` `the claim is about medical advice given by telephone or other telecommunication by a medically qualified person` `in good faith and without recklessness` `within compulsory third party motor vehicle insurance` `significantly impaired by alcohol or another recreational drug` MEANS
    IF NOT (`they expected no payment or other consideration` AND `you were apparently in need of emergency assistance`)
    THEN `s 74 gives no immunity on these facts`
    ELSE IF `within compulsory third party motor vehicle insurance`
         THEN `the immunity does not extend to a liability within compulsory third party motor vehicle insurance (s 74(4)(a))`
         ELSE IF `significantly impaired by alcohol or another recreational drug`
              THEN `the immunity does not operate: their capacity was significantly impaired by alcohol or another recreational drug (s 74(4)(b))`
              ELSE IF `the claim is about medical advice given by telephone or other telecommunication by a medically qualified person`
                   THEN `no: a medically qualified good samaritan incurs no personal civil liability for advice about emergency medical assistance (s 74(3))`
                   ELSE IF `in good faith and without recklessness`
                        THEN `no: a good samaritan incurs no personal civil liability for what was done in good faith and without recklessness (s 74(2))`
                        ELSE `s 74 gives no immunity on these facts`

DECLARE `Apology answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the apology is not an admission of fault or liability, is not relevant to it, and is not admissible as evidence of it (s 75(1), (2))`
    `s 75 does not apply to a defamation claim (s 75(3)(a))`

GIVEN `the claim is in defamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Apology answer`
`the effect of an apology (s 75)` `the claim is in defamation` MEANS
    IF `the claim is in defamation`
    THEN `s 75 does not apply to a defamation claim (s 75(3)(a))`
    ELSE `no: the apology is not an admission of fault or liability, is not relevant to it, and is not admissible as evidence of it (s 75(1), (2))`
